","Gait belt for caregiver-assisted transfers","Automatic blood pressure monitor that also shows pulse, with a written log","Bathroom scale, if the doctor asks for regular weights","Emergency alert pendant that works at home and in the yard, because help may take longer to reach a rural house","Night lights and non-slip footwear","Weekly pill organiser"],"services":[{"name":"Nursing check","detail":"Blood pressure, pulse and weight review, medication check, ankle swelling check, skin check and bruising check.","frequency":"2 visits per week for 6 weeks, then weekly"},{"name":"Physical therapy","detail":"Balance, walking, leg strength and safe use of the walker, at home.","frequency":"3 sessions per week"},{"name":"Occupational therapy","detail":"Right arm and hand, dressing, bathing, kitchen safety and a home safety review.","frequency":"2 sessions per week"},{"name":"Speech-language therapy","detail":"Speech clarity, understanding and swallowing safety. Give her time to answer.","frequency":"2 sessions per week"},{"name":"Personal care","detail":"Stand-by help with washing, dressing and toileting; help getting into bed at night.","frequency":"Twice daily, morning and evening"},{"name":"Medication reminders","detail":"Set up the weekly pill organiser and confirm each dose is taken at the right time. Her heart medicines must not be missed.","frequency":"Daily"},{"name":"Meals","detail":"Heart-healthy, low-salt meals that still give enough protein and energy to keep her strength. Cook, or heat home-delivered meals.","frequency":"Daily"},{"name":"Home safety and emergency check","detail":"House number visible from the road, front light working, phone and alert pendant within reach, clear path for an ambulance.","frequency":"First visit, then monthly"},{"name":"Support for her husband, Arne","detail":"Arne is elderly too. Check that he is coping, eating and getting breaks, and that he does not lift or steady her alone.","frequency":"Each visit"},{"name":"Daily Strovia check-in","detail":"Rate balance, eyes, face, arms and speech, and note when anything started.","frequency":"Once every day"},{"name":"Transport","detail":"Rides to therapy and clinic visits, which are a long way from home. Video visits where the clinic offers them.","frequency":"As scheduled"}],"medications":["Blood-thinning or antiplatelet medicine to help prevent another stroke. Report unusual bruising, nosebleeds or any bleeding","Heart medicines for the heart condition on record: taken exactly as prescribed, never skipped or stopped","Cholesterol-lowering medicine","Blood pressure medicine only if her doctor prescribes it","No diabetes medicine is on record; her blood sugar was normal"],"diet":["Low salt, heart-healthy eating: vegetables, fruit, whole grains, lean protein, little processed food","Enough protein and energy to keep her strength up. Small, frequent meals if she tires. Weigh her weekly and report weight loss","Encourage fluids through the day unless the doctor sets a limit","Sit fully upright to eat; small bites and unhurried meals","Use thickened fluids or softer foods only if the speech-language therapist advises","She stopped smoking. Keep the home smoke-free"],"followUps":[{"who":"Neurology","when":"Every 4 to 6 weeks in the first 3 months"},{"who":"Cardiology","when":"Within 4 weeks, then as directed, for her heart condition and stroke prevention"},{"who":"Primary care","when":"Within 2 weeks of any hospital stay, then every 3 months"},{"who":"Pharmacist medicine review","when":"Once, within 4 weeks, because she takes several medicines"},{"who":"Memory and mood check","when":"Ask the doctor about it; changes in thinking and mood are common after a stroke"},{"who":"Hearing and vision check","when":"If any change is noticed"}],"additional":["The house is in a rural area. An ambulance can take longer to arrive, so keep the phone and alert pendant within her reach and the front light on.","Her husband Arne is 82 and cannot safely lift or steady her. Do not rely on him for transfers.","Her son Erik lives about 40 minutes away and is the first family member to call after the office.","Watch for confusion, low mood or withdrawal and report changes to the office.","Fatigue is expected. Plan rest between therapy sessions.","Encourage her to do as much as she safely can for herself.","Everyone in the home should know the B.E. F.A.S.T. signs and this plan's emergency steps."],"callOfficeIf":["Any change in symptoms — weakness, numbness, speech or vision that is different from usual but not sudden or severe","A new or worsening symptom flagged by Strovia's daily check-in","A fall, even without injury","Missed or refused medication, or a suspected side effect","Blood pressure or blood sugar readings outside the range set by the care team","Coughing or choking during meals, or a wet-sounding voice after drinking","New swelling, redness or pain in a leg or arm","New confusion, low mood, anxiety or a marked change in sleep or appetite","Skin redness or sores where the person sits or lies","A hospital or emergency visit, new prescription, or any change to this care plan","The regular caregiver cannot attend, or equipment is broken or missing","New swelling of the ankles or legs, new breathlessness, or a very slow or very fast pulse","Unusual bruising, nosebleeds or any bleeding (blood-thinning medicine)","She is eating or drinking much less than usual, or is losing weight","Her husband Arne is unwell or cannot cope"],"call911If":["Balance — sudden loss of balance, dizziness or trouble walking","Eyes — sudden vision loss or double vision","Face — one side of the face drooping","Arms — sudden weakness or numbness in an arm or leg","Speech — slurred speech, confusion, or trouble understanding","Time — note when it started, then call 911 straight away","A sudden, severe headache unlike any before","A seizure, or the person cannot be woken","Chest pain, or difficulty breathing","Choking that does not clear, or a fall with a head injury or suspected broken bone"],"review":"Every 30 days, and after any change"}$json$::jsonb
